      "type": "spotlight",
      "item": "tribalpower:waystone_compass",
      "text": [
        "Mark a spot, then come back to it in a blink. A compass remembers one landing floor and carries you there for a little Pulse from a cell in your pack."
      ],
      "title": "Waystone compasses"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Binding and using",
      "text": [
        "Crouch and right-click the **top** of a solid block to bind that floor as your landing.",
        "Right-click in the air to travel. The trip is paid from Pulse Cells anywhere in your inventory, and a **5-second** cooldown follows.",
        "You land standing on the bound floor, so it needs **two clear, dry blocks** above it, and nothing nasty right next to it: fire, lava, magma, cactus, a lit campfire, berry bushes, wither roses or powder snow.",
        "If there is nowhere safe to stand, the trip refuses and spends nothing. Pulse is only taken once the landing is clear. You cannot travel while riding."
      ]
    },
